WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.580 --> 00:00:03.120
Hellboy is here, and it's a total disaster.

00:00:03.340 --> 00:00:07.259
There are a lot of factors behind the failure
of the superhero movie reboot.

00:00:07.259 --> 00:00:10.980
Let's break down why it bombed at the box
office and see if we can nail down just what

00:00:10.980 --> 00:00:14.000
exactly went so wrong with Hellboy 2019.

00:00:14.620 --> 00:00:17.000
The critics have spoken, and they weren't
pleased.

00:00:17.010 --> 00:00:20.970
But most damning for the Hellboy franchise's
future prospects is the fact that this version

00:00:20.970 --> 00:00:23.070
of Big Red didn't make any money at all.

00:00:23.070 --> 00:00:27.470
According to Box Office Mojo, the opening
weekend for Hellboy brought in considerably

00:00:27.470 --> 00:00:30.840
less than even studio Lionsgate's lowest expectations.

00:00:30.840 --> 00:00:35.380
While the studio hoped for at least a $17
million take to start things off for the movie's

00:00:35.380 --> 00:00:41.120
theatrical run, Hellboy instead brought back
only $12 million from more than 3,300 theaters,

00:00:41.120 --> 00:00:44.960
earning a third place at the domestic box
office during its debut.

00:00:44.980 --> 00:00:48.900
All that against a budget that's been reported
to be at least $50 million.

00:00:48.900 --> 00:00:52.380
In other words, it looks like everyone who
backed this project is about to lose their

00:00:52.380 --> 00:00:52.880
money.

00:00:53.180 --> 00:00:53.820
"Oh yeah?"

00:00:54.540 --> 00:00:59.160
Clearly, the world wasn't on fire with anticipation
for a new, rebooted Hellboy movie.

00:00:59.160 --> 00:01:01.620
But not many predicted it would turn out this
bad.

00:01:01.800 --> 00:01:06.380
As reviews rolled in over the movie's opening
weekend, Hellboy's Rotten Tomatoes score hovered

00:01:06.380 --> 00:01:12.250
near the single digits, eventually reaching
a 15% rating with roughly 150 reviews.

00:01:12.250 --> 00:01:15.160
Naturally, the reactions are full of punny
alley-oops.

00:01:15.160 --> 00:01:18.550
The movie is like a personal hell, or at least
the tenth circle of one.

00:01:18.550 --> 00:01:20.540
It's a hell of a headache and a hellish experience.

00:01:20.540 --> 00:01:23.260
It both came from and can go to… you get
it.

00:01:23.260 --> 00:01:25.320
The point is, people hated this movie.

00:01:25.420 --> 00:01:29.500
One of the more understated disses came from
the Associated Press review, which read,

00:01:29.500 --> 00:01:33.420
"So underwhelming was this film that a recent
screening in New York only sparked polite

00:01:33.420 --> 00:01:35.420
applause after it was finally over.

00:01:35.540 --> 00:01:38.530
And that was the red carpet premiere with
all the cast in attendance."

00:01:38.530 --> 00:01:40.220
"Um, are you serious?"

00:01:40.960 --> 00:01:45.100
One of the biggest problems the new Hellboy
failed to overcome is many fans' continuing

00:01:45.100 --> 00:01:48.900
allegiance to the original two movies directed
by Guillermo del Toro.

00:01:49.020 --> 00:01:53.460
Long before this new version of the franchise
was being worked on, del Toro and original

00:01:53.460 --> 00:01:57.240
Hellboy Ron Perlman were ready and willing
to step up for a third act.

00:01:57.240 --> 00:02:01.680
But over the course of the next decade, hopes
for that reunion ever happening slowly faded,

00:02:01.680 --> 00:02:04.680
with producers steering the property toward
a reboot instead.

00:02:05.020 --> 00:02:06.900
"What's my flaw?!"

00:02:07.720 --> 00:02:11.500
What makes the reboot treatment really sting
is less that it happened, and more that Perlman

00:02:11.510 --> 00:02:15.830
and del Toro never stopped trying to make
their version of a third movie a reality.

00:02:15.830 --> 00:02:17.490
Perlman related to Collider in 2018,

00:02:17.490 --> 00:02:22.410
"I spent a long, long time really poking and
prodding the bear to get the third one made,

00:02:22.410 --> 00:02:23.580
and I fell short."

00:02:23.610 --> 00:02:28.180
The results of this gamble on a new direction
were ugly and unprofitable, with the new Hellboy

00:02:28.190 --> 00:02:32.590
grossing considerably less in its opening
weekend than either of its predecessors.

00:02:32.590 --> 00:02:37.480
The franchise's previous movie, 2009's The
Golden Army, went on to a worldwide gross

00:02:37.480 --> 00:02:39.400
of $160 million.

00:02:39.400 --> 00:02:42.280
Good luck reaching those highs again after
a stinker like this.

00:02:42.780 --> 00:02:47.640
If passing over del Toro and Perlman was the
Hellboy reboot's original sin, it didn't necessarily

00:02:47.640 --> 00:02:48.900
damn the entire movie.

00:02:49.020 --> 00:02:53.320
With a unified vision and a great team effort,
things still could've turned out okay.

00:02:53.330 --> 00:02:56.540
But apparently, not everyone making the movie
was on the same team.

00:02:56.540 --> 00:03:01.160
According to a scintillating write-up by TheWrap,
the production of Hellboy 2019 was plagued

00:03:01.160 --> 00:03:04.520
by infighting, disagreements, and even a controversial
firing.

00:03:04.700 --> 00:03:07.040
The specifics of the gossip are frequently
delicious.

00:03:07.040 --> 00:03:11.230
Allegedly, a producer of the movie frequently
stepped on the director's toes, leaving the

00:03:11.230 --> 00:03:14.700
actors with contradictory instructions regarding
how to play scenes.

00:03:14.700 --> 00:03:19.300
Also allegedly, star David Harbour was at
multiple times frustrated enough to simply

00:03:19.300 --> 00:03:21.040
walk off the set during shooting.

00:03:21.220 --> 00:03:24.850
The report also claims that the script was
being re-written during production, which

00:03:24.850 --> 00:03:28.290
might help to explain the story's overall
disjointed feel.

00:03:28.290 --> 00:03:32.480
It's easy to see how an atmosphere like this
could lead to the creation of a subpar movie.

00:03:32.680 --> 00:03:36.599
But whatever the reasons behind it being lousy
are, we're sure there are plenty of people

00:03:36.600 --> 00:03:37.840
who might just want their money back.

00:03:38.600 --> 00:03:43.140
Comic book series can exist for years or even
decades before getting a shot on the big screen,

00:03:43.140 --> 00:03:47.599
often spooling out whole encyclopedias' worth
of confusing lore in the process.

00:03:47.599 --> 00:03:52.420
As a result, it's extremely easy for adaptations
to fall into the trap of becoming over-complicated

00:03:52.420 --> 00:03:57.370
messes with too much story, too many characters,
or simply too much weird crap going on for

00:03:57.370 --> 00:03:59.269
a general audience to get on board with.

00:03:59.269 --> 00:04:03.819
According to many reviews, Hellboy's biggest
problem is how over-complicated and confusing

00:04:03.820 --> 00:04:08.280
its plot developments can be, with important
characters remaining strangely two-dimensional

00:04:08.340 --> 00:04:11.720
while the movie wastes time with cameos and
comic book references.

00:04:11.730 --> 00:04:15.170
While parts of the movie that may delight
readers of the comic books with satisfaction

00:04:15.170 --> 00:04:20.289
of the "oh, I recognize that" variety, they
might come off to casual fans as weird, momentum-killing

00:04:20.289 --> 00:04:21.359
digressions.

00:04:21.359 --> 00:04:24.710
Even people who know the comics might not
be able to get around the movie's breathless

00:04:24.710 --> 00:04:26.529
pace and stunning density.

00:04:26.529 --> 00:04:30.340
In trying to include so much, the movie succeeds
in conveying very little.

00:04:30.340 --> 00:04:31.809
And it's a superhero movie!

00:04:31.809 --> 00:04:34.389
All it needed to be was "good guys vs. bad
guys."

00:04:34.389 --> 00:04:36.500
How the heck do you go about screwing that
up?

00:04:36.920 --> 00:04:41.400
Out of the people who did see Hellboy, enough
walked away agitated enough to saddle it with

00:04:41.409 --> 00:04:42.701
an abysmal C rating at Cinemascore.

00:04:42.701 --> 00:04:47.830
While a C may come off as average, it's actually
quite lousy for a movie like this.

00:04:47.830 --> 00:04:52.150
A Cinemascore rating reflects the results
of theatrical exit polls, with regular people

00:04:52.150 --> 00:04:56.099
leaving opening night screenings basically
being asked if they liked what they saw and

00:04:56.100 --> 00:04:57.060
got what they paid for.

00:04:57.100 --> 00:05:01.700
Movies for general audiences tend to easily
get As and Bs, while lower ratings are often

00:05:01.710 --> 00:05:05.349
more reserved for horror movies, which tend
to be unconventional by nature.

00:05:05.349 --> 00:05:09.180
While Hellboy certainly has its horror elements,
it's more aspiring to be the same kind of

00:05:09.180 --> 00:05:13.729
beast as Deadpool, playing as a crowd-pleasing,
four-quadrant blockbuster with some blood

00:05:13.729 --> 00:05:15.140
and guts and naughty words.

00:05:15.180 --> 00:05:19.340
That's what the movie sold itself as, but
a C Cinemascore suggests that people did not

00:05:19.340 --> 00:05:21.070
get what they wanted out of Hellboy.

00:05:21.070 --> 00:05:25.889
Whether it was too gory, too confusing, or
just too weird, it also suggests that people

00:05:25.889 --> 00:05:29.410
won't be running to tell their friends to
go see it either, meaning any hopes of the

00:05:29.410 --> 00:05:33.069
movie picking up speed in the weeks after
its debut are pretty low, especially with

00:05:33.069 --> 00:05:34.789
the Avengers right around the corner.

00:05:34.789 --> 00:05:37.249
At that point, it's curtains for ol' Hellboy.

00:05:37.249 --> 00:05:40.530
In hindsight, they probably should've just
let Guillermo finish his trilogy.

00:05:40.530 --> 00:05:42.920
It couldn't have turned out much worse than
this.

